 0 in output has (\"world\", \"!\")\n- Position 1 in output has (\"Hello\", \"\")\n\nSo both lists are just reversed independently, which is what the example shows. Let me code this up by reversing each list separately and returning them as a tuple.\n\nBut I should verify the logic handles edge cases properly—empty elements or punctuation lists work fine with the same approach.",
